Description: pvr: winsys support for firmware job timestamps
 Copy the uAPI of a7s-linux-lts (drm-imagination-firmware-timestamps-around-jobs)
 into include/drm-uapi/pvr_drm.h: the query DRM_PVR_DEV_QUERY_TIMESTAMP_INFO_GET
 (0x100), the buffer flag DRM_PVR_BO_FW_TIMESTAMPS and the timestamp fields at the
 end of struct drm_pvr_job. The powervr winsys asks the query once; a kernel that
 does not know it fails it and the winsys reports no support. The winsys passes
 the buffer flag (PVR_WINSYS_BO_FLAG_FW_TIMESTAMPS) and, for compute jobs, the
 timestamps asked for in pvr_winsys_compute_submit_info. The buffer flag is bit 32,
 so pvr_drm_create_gem_bo() now takes the flags as 64 bits. struct drm_pvr_job is
 copied by the kernel with copy_struct_from_user(), so the longer struct with
 zeroed timestamp fields is accepted by a kernel without them.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
